From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 08:39:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Budget open layers by depth, not cumulative pushes

LayerManager checked `layers_used` against LAYER_LIMIT, but
`layers_used` is only ever incremented: `maybe_pop_layer` gives back
`layer_depth` and never `layers_used`. The check therefore capped the
total number of clips a paint pass may ever push, not how many are open
at once, so a heavy page exhausts it partway through and every later
clip is silently refused. A refused clip does not skip its content; it
paints it unclipped. On a page scrolled to the bottom, 1x1
`clip: rect(0,0,0,0)` screen-reader spans inside a fixed header painted
their text over the page. Fixed subtrees are hoisted and painted last,
which is why they were the ones left without budget.

Depth is also the quantity worth bounding: each open layer costs the
rasterizer a scratch buffer, and a pop releases it. 1024 concurrently
open layers is still far beyond anything real content nests.

Also fix the depth high-water mark, which read
`layer_depth.max(layer_depth)` (a no-op) instead of writing the
`layer_depth_used` field that exists for it.
---
 src/layers.rs | 21 ++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/layers.rs b/src/layers.rs
index bd1b4e7..c4c0d67 100644
--- a/src/layers.rs
+++ b/src/layers.rs
@@ -7,11 +7,15 @@ const LAYER_LIMIT: u32 = 1024;

 #[derive(Default)]
 pub(crate) struct LayerManager {
-    layers_used: Cell<u32>,
     layer_depth: Cell<u32>,
-    layers_wanted: Cell<u32>,

-    #[allow(unused)] // Only used for debugging. Enabled as required.
+    // Diagnostics only. layers_wanted minus layers_used is how many layers
+    // LAYER_LIMIT refused; layer_depth_used is the depth high-water mark.
+    #[allow(unused)]
+    layers_used: Cell<u32>,
+    #[allow(unused)]
+    layers_wanted: Cell<u32>,
+    #[allow(unused)]
     layer_depth_used: Cell<u32>,
 }

@@ -57,9 +61,11 @@ impl LayerManager {
         }
         self.layers_wanted.update(|x| x + 1);

-        // Check if clips are above limit
-        let layers_available = self.layers_used.get() <= LAYER_LIMIT;
-        if !layers_available {
+        // Budget concurrently-open layers, not the running total: each open
+        // layer costs the rasterizer a scratch buffer, and pops give that back.
+        // Counting every push ever made exhausts the budget partway through a
+        // heavy page, and a refused clip then paints its content unclipped.
+        if self.layer_depth.get() >= LAYER_LIMIT {
             return false;
         }

@@ -81,7 +87,8 @@ impl LayerManager {
         // Update accounting
         self.layers_used.update(|x| x + 1);
         self.layer_depth.update(|x| x + 1);
-        self.layer_depth.update(|x| x.max(self.layer_depth.get()));
+        self.layer_depth_used
+            .update(|x| x.max(self.layer_depth.get()));

         true
     }
